Hints: $\sin x+\cos x=\min _{x \in I R}\left\{1, a^2-4 a+6\right\}$
$$
\begin{aligned}
& a^2-4 a+6=(a-2)^2+2 \therefore \min _{a \in I R}\left(a^2-4 a+6\right)=2 \\
& \therefore \min _{a \in I R}\left\{1, a^2-4 a+6\right\}=\min \{1,2\}=1 \\
& \sin x+\cos x=1 \Rightarrow \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \sin x+\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \cos x=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\
& \Rightarrow \sin \left(x+\frac{\pi}{4}\right)=\sin \frac{\pi}{4}, \Rightarrow x+\frac{\pi}{4}=n \pi+(-1)^n \cdot \frac{\pi}{4}
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\Rightarrow x=n \pi+(-1)^n \frac{\pi}{4}-\frac{\pi}{4}
$$
